Hello everyone,

>From Bakka et al  (Spatial modeling with R-INLA: A review, 2018):
"...a restriction with the SPDE approach is that it is only computable if α is an integer..."

>From INLA documentation (https://rdrr.io/github/andrewzm/INLA/man/inla.spde2.matern.html):
"Stationary models are supported for 0 < α ≤q 2, with spectral approximation methods used for non-integer α"

Where can I learn about how the spectral approximation method is used in the context of INLA?

(Basically, I fit a bunch of models and half of them use alpha=3/2, so I'm wondering what I built the mesh for!)

Best,

Mark

